SUMMARY:Corn Hole Tournament at AMB
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Social Club\n**Hey y’all!! We’re gonna host a Co
 rn Hole Tournament at Appalachian Mountain Brewery!**\n**We’re gonna hos
 t a double elimination tournament!** **AMB has four cornhole board sets\, 
 and several of us have more. We’re going to run eight games at a time if
  needed.** **Come out and let’s have some fun\,** **and support a great 
 local business!**\n\n**Grab your partner and come out and play! If you do 
 not have a partner\, you can** **partner with someone at the event.** **Do
  not let not having a partner stop you from coming out for this event.**\n
 \n**Be there at 5:00 to register teams of two\, or to find a partner at th
 e event. Registration closes at 5:45. First games start at 6:00.**\n\n**We
  are going to have two brackets.**\n\n**Competition**\n\n**Fun**\n\n* **Co
 mpetition bracket will be a paid bracket that will have a $10 entry fee pe
 r team of two. There will be prizes for 1st\, 2nd and 3rd place winners.**
 \n\n* **Fun bracket will be for teams or individuals that want to particip
 ate\, but not be in the running for prizes.**\n\n**Brackets close when we 
 reach 12 teams in each.**\n**So sign up and get your team’s spot!**\n\n*
 *When you sign up for the event\, please post a comment stating whether yo
 u want to do competition or fun bracket. The $10 will be accepted the day 
 of the event.**\n\n**https://www.amb.beer/mills-river**\n\n**This is gonna
  be fun!!**\n\n**The object of cornhole is to reach exactly 21 points firs
 t. Teams score points by tossing bags onto the board (1 point) or through 
 the hole (3 points). Play alternates until all 8 bags are tossed\, and sco
 res cancel each other out at the end of each round (cancellation scoring).
 Setup &**\n\n**GameplayDistance: Place boards 27 feet apart (measured from
  the front edge to the front edge). For a casual backyard game\, you can a
 djust this distance based on player ability.**\n\n**Teams: Played with 2 p
 layers (Singles) or 4 players (Doubles). In doubles\, teammates stand dire
 ctly across from each other at opposite boards.**\n\n**Turns: Players thro
 w underhand and must stay behind the foul line (the front edge of the boar
 d). Players alternate turns throwing one bag at a time until all 8 bags ha
 ve been tossed.**\n\n**Scoring: in the hole: 3 points. On the board: 1 poi
 nt. Foul bag: 0 points (e.g.\, if a bag hits the ground first or if a play
 er steps on or crosses the foul line).Points are calculated using cancella
 tion scoring.**\n\n**The team with the higher score in the round subtracts
  the lower team's score to get the net points for that round. For example\
 , if Team A scores 5 points and Team B scores 3 points\, Team A is awarded
  2 points for that frame.**
